          }
        }
      }
    },
    "rhr.detail.about.baseline.body" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Resting heart rate varies enormously between people — 45 bpm can be ordinary for one athlete and unusually low for another. Tuwa compares you only against your own rolling 7-day average, so the number that matters is the deviation, not the reading."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "不同人的静息心率差异极大——45 次/分对一个运动员可能很平常，对另一个人则异常地低。Tuwa 只将你与自己的 7 日滚动平均值比较，所以真正重要的是偏离幅度，而不是数据本身的高低。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "rhr.detail.about.baseline.title" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Why your baseline is personal"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "为什么基准线因人而异"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "rhr.detail.about.direction.body" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Resting heart rate reads the opposite way to HRV: a rise above your baseline is the fatigue direction, a fall is the rested one. One raised morning is usually noise — alcohol, a late meal, a hard session the day before. Two or three in a row alongside a falling HRV is the pattern, and that is what your readiness score is already weighing."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "静息心率的方向与心率变异性相反：高于基准线是疲劳的方向，低于基准线是恢复的方向。单次升高通常只是噪音——饮酒、晚餐吃太晚、前一天练得重。连续两三次且伴随心率变异性下降，才是真正的模式，而这正是你的准备度评分在监测的内容。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "rhr.detail.about.direction.title" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Which direction matters"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "哪个方向值得注意"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "rhr.detail.about.measures.title" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "What resting heart rate measures"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "静息心率是在测量什么"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "rhr.detail.about.window.body" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Apple Watch computes resting heart rate as a daily figure over your rest periods and refines it through the day, so its timestamp does not mark a morning reading. Tuwa therefore takes one value per calendar day with no time-of-day filter. HRV is the opposite — a momentary measurement whose time of day changes what it means — and keeps its morning window."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Apple Watch 会在你的休息时段上计算出一个每日静息心率，并在一天中不断修正，所以它的时间戳并不代表这是一个晨间读数。因此 Tuwa 每个日历日只取一个值，不做时段筛选。心率变异性正好相反——它是瞬时测量，测量时间会改变它的含义——所以它保留晨间窗口。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "rhr.detail.about.window.title" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Why this uses the whole day"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "为什么使用整天的数据"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "rhr.detail.delta.vsAvg" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ vs 7-day avg"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%@ 相对 7 日平均"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "rhr.detail.explanation" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Resting heart rate is the lowest sustained rate your heart holds while you are at rest. A lower figure usually means better recovery. The dashed line shows your 7-day rolling average."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "静息心率是你在休息状态下心脏维持的最低持续心率。数值越低通常表示恢复越好。虚线显示你的 7 日滚动平均值。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
